  "term": "cri du chat syndrome",
  "definition": "Cri du chat syndrome is a genetic condition in infancy caused by loss of part of the short arm of chromosome 5. It is known for a high-pitched cry resembling a cat’s and commonly involves poor growth, a small head, major intellectual impairment, muscle stiffness and weakness affecting all four limbs, and several facial and genital differences.",
